            <div xml:id="d621">

                <pb facs="0711" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660c.116/39</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Poland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stetson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                        1927</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 18.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1125</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    situation regarding the importation of American automobiles into Poland has
                    become so vexatious that I have sent a note on the subject, copy of which is
                    enclosed, to the Polish Foreign Office requesting that a contingent for
                    automobiles be allotted as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>While I am not particularly hopeful of obtaining any tangible result from this
                    note I felt that it was necessary in the protection of American interests to go
                    on record at this time.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Stetson</hi>,
                    Jr.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d621-a1.xml" xpointer="d621-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
